module rawframe.model

// 3D pictures as World data (SPEC-0024's scene, D283): what an entity
// shows, drawn where its pose (rawframe.physics3d's Pose3D) puts it, lit
// by the sun and the sky. A game declares components of these types;
// clients draw them, and a server carries them as it carries any other
// value, with no drawing of its own.

// A mesh drawn at the pose: the game's cooked mesh of the identity its
// `mesh` line gives it, or one of the engine's own below, scaled by
// `scaleX`, `scaleY`, and `scaleZ` along the pose's own axes, and turned
// as the pose turns. `material` is the game's surface material of the
// identity its `material` line gives it (D303), or nought for none: a
// plain surface, OpenPBR's but for a white base color. `color`, 0xRRGGBBAA
// in sRGB, tints the material's base color, so without one it is the base
// color; an alpha of nought, a scale of nought, or mesh nought draws
// nothing.
struct Model {
    mesh: u64
    scaleX: f32
    scaleY: f32
    scaleZ: f32
    color: u32
    material: u64
}

// The engine's own meshes, each one meter from its center to its sides,
// so a Model's scale is the body's (rawframe.physics3d's Body3D) half
// sides or radius: a box of half sides one; a sphere of radius one; an
// upright cylinder of radius one and half height one; an upright capsule
// of radius one whose two centers are one above and below its center (a
// scale along its axis stretches its caps too).
const BOX: u64 = 0x3ff8cd61f01cf46b
const SPHERE: u64 = 0x2c6b82d75f7be712
const CYLINDER: u64 = 0xaee26a717a3a62a0
const CAPSULE: u64 = 0x63ed148327123836

// A client's view of the 3D World (ADR-0052's camera), on the client's
// own player: a presentation component (`presentation <camera> on
// player`) its present systems place. The eye is `offsetX`, `offsetY`,
// and `offsetZ` meters from the player's pose, in the World's axes, and
// looks along `yaw` radians about +Y (nought looks along -Z, a quarter
// turn along -X) and `pitch` radians above the ground's plane. `fovY` is
// the vertical field of view in radians (a wider window sees more,
// Hor+), and `near` the nearest distance drawn, in meters; the far one is
// unbounded. `exposure` is the camera's EV100 (ADR-0047): 15 for a sunny
// day, lower for dimmer scenes. `tonemapper` maps its light for display
// (ADR-0047's closed set): AGX (nought, the default), PBR_NEUTRAL for
// colours reproduced as authored, or LINEAR for measuring; each keeps
// middle grey where AgX puts it, and another value is AgX. A camera with a
// field of view not above nought draws nothing. Without one, a client's
// view looks at its player from behind and above.
struct Camera {
    offsetX: f32
    offsetY: f32
    offsetZ: f32
    yaw: f32
    pitch: f32
    fovY: f32
    near: f32
    exposure: f32
    tonemapper: u32
}

// The tonemappers a camera may map its light with (ADR-0047).
const AGX: u32 = 0
const PBR_NEUTRAL: u32 = 1
const LINEAR: u32 = 2

// A camera's grading (ADR-0051, ADR-0047), on the same entity as its
// camera: the scene's light, before it is mapped for display, balanced to
// a white `temperature` warmer (above nought) or cooler and `tint` more
// magenta (above nought) or green, about minus one to one; then each
// channel times its `slope`, plus its `offset`, to the power of its
// `power` (ASC CDL); then `saturation` (one keeps it, nought is grey) and
// `contrast` about middle grey (one keeps it). One with a power not above
// nought grades nothing: a grade not yet set is all nought.
struct Grading {
    slopeR: f32
    slopeG: f32
    slopeB: f32
    offsetR: f32
    offsetG: f32
    offsetB: f32
    powerR: f32
    powerG: f32
    powerB: f32
    saturation: f32
    contrast: f32
    temperature: f32
    tint: f32
}

// A camera's exposure metered from what it sees (ADR-0051, ADR-0047), on
// the same entity as its camera, whose `exposure` it starts from: the
// frame's light measured in a histogram of its luminance, the darkest
// `low` and the brightest past `high` of its pixels (fractions, nought to
// one) left out, the rest averaged into an EV100 less `compensation`
// stops, kept between `minimum` and `maximum`, and reached at `brighten`
// EV a second when the picture must brighten and `darken` when it must
// darken; at once when the metering starts or the eye cuts away. One
// whose maximum is not above its minimum meters nothing. Without one, the
// camera's `exposure` holds.
struct AutoExposure {
    minimum: f32
    maximum: f32
    brighten: f32
    darken: f32
    compensation: f32
    low: f32
    high: f32
}

// The sun (ADR-0051's directional light), on any entity: light arriving
// along the direction (`directionX`, `directionY`, `directionZ`), the way
// it travels, `illuminance` lux on a surface facing it (about 100,000 at
// noon), in `color` (0xRRGGBBAA, sRGB; alpha unused). A game declares at
// most one sun; without one, a sun at noon lights the World.
struct Sun {
    directionX: f32
    directionY: f32
    directionZ: f32
    illuminance: f32
    color: u32
}

// The sky's light, arriving from above the horizon (ADR-0051's ambient
// term): `luminance` candela per square meter (about 5,000 on a clear
// day), in `color`. From below it comes what the ground gives back of the
// sun's light and the sky's (D304): `ground` is its albedo, 0xRRGGBBAA in
// sRGB (alpha unused), and nought gives nothing back. A game declares at
// most one; without one, a clear day's: 5,000 in a clear blue
// (0x8FB8EBFF) over a ground giving back a fifth (0x7C7C7CFF).
struct Sky {
    luminance: f32
    color: u32
    ground: u32
}

// A point light (ADR-0051), on any entity, at its pose: `lumens` of
// luminous power spread evenly (a lumen over 4π is a candela), reaching
// `range` meters, where it has faded to nought, in `color` (0xRRGGBBAA,
// sRGB; alpha unused). Lumens or a range of nought light nothing. With
// `shadows`, what stands between it and a surface shades it, for as many
// lights as the view's budget holds, those covering most of it first.
struct PointLight {
    lumens: f32
    range: f32
    color: u32
    shadows: bool
}

// A spot light (ADR-0051), on any entity, at its pose, shining along the
// pose's -Z (nought turn shines along -Z, as a camera looks): `lumens` as
// if all of them lay in its cone (a lumen over π is a candela, ADR-0051's
// documented approximation), full within `inner` radians of its axis and
// fading to nought at `outer`, reaching `range` meters, in `color`; with
// `shadows`, shadowed as a point light is.
struct SpotLight {
    lumens: f32
    range: f32
    inner: f32
    outer: f32
    color: u32
    shadows: bool
}

// White: a surface, a sun, or a sky as it is.
const WHITE: u32 = 0xFFFFFFFF
